---
title: Baked Apple Cider Donuts
description: Baked, cakey, and delicious apple cider donuts are made with apple cider reduction to intensify its flavor. Warm and dipped in cinnamon sugar and apple pie spices, this fall treat will become your new favorite too.
image: https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/apple-cider-doughnuts-225x225.jpg
source: https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/baked-apple-cider-donuts/
author: Sally
time required: 1 hour
cook time: 10 minutes
course: Breakfast
servings: 12
cuisine: American
prep time: 45 minutes
---

== Donuts ==

Simmer @apple cider{1.5%cups} in a #small saucepan{} over low heat, stirring occasionally, until you’re left with about 1/2 cup. Start checking at ~{10%minutes}, then every 5 minutes, until you have the reduced amount. It realistically will take around 20 minutes though. If there are any spices or solids on top of your reduced apple cider, leave them. Set aside to cool for ~{10%minutes}.

Preheat #oven to 350°F. Spray #donut pan{} with non-stick spray. Set aside.

Whisk together @all-purpose flour{2%cups}, @baking soda{1%tsp}, @baking powder{3/4%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{1%tsp}, @apple pie spice{1%tsp}, and @salt{1/4%tsp} in a #large bowl{}. Set aside.

In another #bowl, whisk together @butter{2%tbsp}(unsalted, melted), @egg{1}(large, at room temperature), @brown sugar{1/2%cup}(packed), @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}, @milk{1/2%cup}(substitute buttermilk, at room temperature), and @vanilla extract{1%tsp}. Pour this mixture into the dry ingredients, add the reduced apple cider, and whisk everything together until smooth and combined. The batter will be slightly thick.

Spoon the batter into the donut mold. You should aim to fill it about halfway.

Bake for ~{10-11%minutes} or until the edges and tops are lightly browned. To test, poke your finger into the top of the donut. If the donut bounces back, they're done. Cool donuts for ~{2%minutes} then transfer to a wire rack. Re-grease the pan and bake the remaining donut batter.

== Toppings ==

Combine @granulated sugar{200%g}, @ground cinnamon{3/4%tsp}, and @apple pie spice{3/4%tsp} together in a medium bowl. Once cool enough to handle, dunk both sides of each donut in @butter{6%tbsp}(unsalted, melted), then generously in the apple spice topping.